jmp-ai-music-player (1.1.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Media keys control the player: play/pause, next, previous and stop.
    The native window publishes an MPRIS player, so the desktop's own keys
    reach it even in the background; the focused window also handles the
    keysyms itself, and a browser window handles them while focused.
  * No tag, playlist or audio file is touched: every key becomes the same
    POST /api/transport call as the matching transport button.

 -- Julian M. Kunkel <julian.kunkel@gwdg.de>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:20:00 +0100

jmp-ai-music-player (1.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New Settings tab "Profile": see what the app learned about you — every
    artist, genre, mood and keyword weight with the bounded influence that
    selection really applies, plus notes, learned phrases, recent plays and
    the events that changed them.  Read-only.
  * The now-playing header keeps its label on its own line and fits all nine
    icon buttons below it, wrapping instead of overflowing on a narrow
    sidebar.
  * "What have you learned" in chat points at the new Profile page.

 -- Julian M. Kunkel <julian.kunkel@gwdg.de>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:10:00 +0100

jmp-ai-music-player (1.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Window opens at 1440x960 and refuses to shrink below 1024x640, so the
    settings tabs and the sticky Save row are never clipped.
  * Diagnostics shows the absolute server start time and can clean up its
    logs from the panel (the old content is kept as .1).
  * Find songs with similar lyrics: a TF-IDF word comparison over the stored
    lyric lines, no model and no audio read.
  * Fixes a TypeError in the mpv error message when a command carried a
    float argument.

 -- Julian M. Kunkel <julian.kunkel@gwdg.de>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:30:00 +0100

jmp-ai-music-player (1.1.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Endless mode: the queue grows from the track that just played and
    repeats itself when nothing fitting is left.
  * Shuffle mode: arm random order for every playlist that starts.
  * Fixes a transport crash on fractional values ("Unknown format 'd'
    for object of type 'float'" on a seek), hardens volume, position and
    speed parsing, and fixes the optional download module search path.

 -- Julian M. Kunkel <julian.kunkel@gwdg.de>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0100

jmp-ai-music-player (1.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian/Ubuntu package.
  * Installs the player, the chat window, the CLI and the documentation.
  * Uses the distribution's Python 3, python3-mutagen and python3-numpy.
  * No download feature: only builds with an optional download module have it.

 -- Julian M. Kunkel <julian.kunkel@gwdg.de>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
